WEBVTT

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:06.260
Sieg Zeon, Sieg Zeon,
Sieg Zeon...

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:09.720
The coordinates
displayed by the La+ Program

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:13.380
point to Torrington base in Australia,
where a colony once fell.

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:15.680
Banagher, shoot while you can!

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:18.510
I can't shoot!

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:24.970
Despite their mutual Newtype resonance,

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:28.720
Banagher is unable to save Loni Garvey
from the curse of her blood ties.

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:30.090
While still in despair,

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:32.970
Banagher is suddenly attacked
by a black Unicorn Gundam.

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:12.220
Attention, incoming VC202!

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:15.840
This is Torrington Control.
State your affiliation and objective.

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:17.220
Torrington Control,

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:19.970
we are a transport
belonging to the Vist Foundation,

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:22.300
on a special mission
from Staff Headquarters.

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:24.380
We are now delivering
a prototype mobile suit.

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:26.930
We're sending it to you on a Base Jabber.

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:29.470
Transmitting operation code
from Staff Headquarters.

00:02:29.630 --> 00:02:33.050
Operation code received.
Special mission queried and confirmed.

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:34.340
Approaching Base Jabber,

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:37.300
descend to regulation altitude.
We'll guide you into final approach course.

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:40.260
Now commencing mission.
Detaching suit... and deploying!

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:42.970
Mission? What mission?!

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:45.550
Hey! Approaching Base Jabber!

00:02:45.590 --> 00:02:47.220
Follow our control instructions!

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:50.630
I repeat, follow our control instructions!

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:07.220
A black...

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:10.880
Unicorn...?

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:16.130
Is it a friendly?

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:22.430
No!

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:56.260
Get out of there, Banagher!

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:06.720
(BANAGHER LINKS, SOLDIER)

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:25.800
The hatch won't open.

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:29.090
I thought I gave you the release code!
Drag him out of there right now!

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:32.800
Hey, what are you doing here?
What's that black Unicorn?!

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:39.550
Oh, you mean the Banshee. The situation
is more complicated than I can explain.

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:41.470
Get a move on!

00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:42.510
Hold it!

00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:03.590
This is also a family matter.

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:08.380
Not even the military has the right to
meddle in family business, don't you agree?

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:10.340
What do you mean, family?

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:14.510
It's rather embarrassing, really,
but he, Banagher Links,

00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:19.130
is the illegitimate son of the previous
head of the family, Cardeas Vist.

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:23.340
As such, I would appreciate
your not inquiring further.

00:06:24.470 --> 00:06:25.550
Banagher is- -

00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:27.180
The hatch is opening.

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:53.380
It's refusing all external commands, and
the system has gone completely dormant.

00:06:55.800 --> 00:06:56.880
And?

00:06:56.930 --> 00:07:01.680
Our guess is that Banagher Links
put some sort of block in place.

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:04.760
Without confirmation from him,
we won't be able to obtain

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:07.930
the new information
disclosed by the La+ Program.

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:12.760
Perhaps it's in his blood.
Did you know about him?

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:20.430
No. I was already away at
boarding school when he was born.

00:07:20.470 --> 00:07:21.510
I can't believe that boy is- -

00:07:21.550 --> 00:07:23.840
He certainly has the
same stubborn streak.

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:29.800
It appears that we should
get her to convince him.

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:40.220
Audrey Burne.

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:44.840
As assumed names go,
it has a lovely ring to it.

00:07:45.720 --> 00:07:50.130
This means that Chairman Ronan Marcenas
is aware of my transfer, I take it?

00:07:50.180 --> 00:07:51.340
Of course.

00:07:52.130 --> 00:07:56.300
We are working towards
the same goal as Chairman Ronan.

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:10.050
We will seal Laplace's Box for good.

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:13.800
I believe that you left Neo Zeon because
you wished for the same thing, Highness.

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:17.300
Any time now, the Unicorn Gundam,
the box's key,

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:19.590
will be delivered to this Garuda.

00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:23.510
Until that time, the young pilot
will act as its guardian.

00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:29.630
This boy is no stranger to you, Highness?
Banagher Links.

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:33.180
Apparently, he locked the coordinate data
that was revealed during yesterday's battle

00:08:33.220 --> 00:08:35.590
and is keeping it hidden.

00:08:35.630 --> 00:08:39.720
The bastard son inherits the sad delusions
of the foolish father...

00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:42.630
You have no idea how much
trouble he is causing us.

00:08:44.130 --> 00:08:47.130
That man was... Banagher's...

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:56.720
Might I persuade you to work
with me, Princess Mineva?

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:01.630
You want me to win
Banagher over for you?

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:03.840
I will make it worth your while.

00:09:03.880 --> 00:09:08.050
I will also guarantee a place for the
Zeon remnants who accompany you.

00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:12.680
In that case, I want you to return
Marida Cruz first.

00:09:13.510 --> 00:09:20.840
Lt. Marida, Ple Twelve, is working
for us of her own free will.

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:23.260
You forced her to undergo
reconditioning...

00:09:23.300 --> 00:09:28.340
Yes, we reconditioned her.
Just as the Neo Zeon once did.

00:09:29.180 --> 00:09:33.260
We weren't the ones who created
that poor creature.

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:38.180
I simply unleashed
what was within her

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:41.090
and gave her the opportunity
to exact her revenge.

00:09:41.130 --> 00:09:42.260
Revenge?

00:09:42.300 --> 00:09:46.760
Yes, revenge against the world
that created things such as her.

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:50.800
A world ruled by the logic of men.

00:10:05.220 --> 00:10:09.510
If you don't give us the bare minimum
of information, we can't protect the ship.

00:10:09.550 --> 00:10:12.720
We can't stand being pushed
around by those civilians!

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:16.630
At this time, we are working under the
direction of General Staff Headquarters.

00:10:16.680 --> 00:10:19.050
Think of the Foundation
as part of them.

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:25.340
Londo Bell's mission has not changed.

00:10:25.380 --> 00:10:27.300
The job of this vessel for now

00:10:27.340 --> 00:10:30.760
is to hunt down
the Neo Zeon ship that infiltrated Earth.

00:10:30.800 --> 00:10:35.380
That said, there can be no denying that
the initial state of affairs has changed.

00:10:41.880 --> 00:10:45.590
We will launch the captured Gundam type
into space via shuttle.

00:10:45.630 --> 00:10:49.180
Once that is done, the Vist Foundation
personnel will also leave this ship.

00:10:49.220 --> 00:10:50.930
Regardless of any objections you may have,

00:10:50.970 --> 00:10:53.430
I expect you to refrain
from any rash behavior.

00:10:53.470 --> 00:10:54.800
Dismissed!

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:04.590
They say that everything shipped
to the Garuda was fit for royalty.

00:11:04.630 --> 00:11:07.970
So, just as the intel from Luio & Co. said.

00:11:08.010 --> 00:11:09.760
Can I speak to him?

00:11:09.800 --> 00:11:14.380
They approved it right away. Please
assume that the walls have ears, sir.

00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:16.840
And here I thought
this was my ship...

00:11:35.180 --> 00:11:38.130
I'd like a quick word.
Is that all right?

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:46.010
I'm Bright Noah. I'm the captain
of the Ra Cailum.

00:11:47.510 --> 00:11:49.970
You seem to be giving the interrogators
no end of trouble.

00:11:52.380 --> 00:11:55.630
Both you and the suit
are keeping your lips sealed.

00:11:55.680 --> 00:11:58.510
Our technical staff are
tearing their hair out.

00:11:59.340 --> 00:12:01.550
I can't let anyone see them.

00:12:02.340 --> 00:12:06.130
If people learn what they are, that place
will become a battlefield again

00:12:06.180 --> 00:12:08.220
and lots of people will die.

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:10.300
Just like Ms. Loni.

00:12:10.340 --> 00:12:13.590
Go ahead and keep them to yourself.

00:12:15.180 --> 00:12:17.970
Did you escape from that camouflaged
freighter to get here?

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:21.010
"Escaped" isn't the right word.

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:23.720
I think of it as them
sending me on my way.

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:28.930
The Captain didn't exactly
agree to that operation.

00:12:28.970 --> 00:12:34.010
I don't doubt it. I got that impression
from the actions of that ship.

00:12:34.050 --> 00:12:37.220
You weren't being treated
as a prisoner.

00:12:37.970 --> 00:12:41.550
Does that mean you were free
to act as you pleased?

00:12:41.590 --> 00:12:43.430
Yes, I was.

00:12:43.470 --> 00:12:48.010
I didn't get the sense we were enemies
like the Federation says we are.

00:12:48.050 --> 00:12:49.550
Why was that?

00:12:49.590 --> 00:12:52.380
Because I'm not a soldier.

00:12:52.430 --> 00:12:55.630
I'm not used to lumping people
into "friend" or "foe".

00:12:56.430 --> 00:13:01.050
But aboard that ship, it felt like
there wasn't any need to.

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:04.380
I see.

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:08.550
I understand now.
Thank you.

00:13:12.050 --> 00:13:13.930
Don't give up.

00:13:13.970 --> 00:13:16.300
I see strength in your eyes.

00:13:16.340 --> 00:13:19.340
Strong eyes that can
feed off of adversity.

00:13:19.380 --> 00:13:20.760
As long as you don't give up,

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:22.590
you'll be able to seize
whatever opportunities come along.

00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:26.180
I don't have strength like that.

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:28.130
It's all just dumb luck.

00:13:28.180 --> 00:13:31.430
Me piloting the Unicorn.
Me ending up here like this...

00:13:31.470 --> 00:13:33.260
Is it really?

00:13:34.590 --> 00:13:39.050
When you first encountered the Gundam,
it might have been mere luck.

00:13:39.590 --> 00:13:43.510
It's been that way for every pilot
of a Gundam up until now.

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:47.430
However, the decision of whether or not to
get into that Gundam rested with you alone.

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:49.680
Luck had nothing to do with that.

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:51.300
Am I wrong?

00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:57.220
At that moment, what was it that
gave you the resolve to pilot it?

00:14:03.630 --> 00:14:05.340
There's someone that I want to help.

00:14:06.880 --> 00:14:08.550
Audrey Burne.

00:14:10.380 --> 00:14:13.590
She's the girl that everyone
calls Mineva Zabi.

00:14:22.340 --> 00:14:25.800
Are you sure? The General Revil
has been mobilized?

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:28.180
Apparently, it received orders straight
from Gen. Staff HQ

00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:30.130
during its shakedown cruise.

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:32.800
They clearly want it to carry out
some sort of covert operation, don't they?

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:36.010
They're after the Nahel Argama...

00:14:36.050 --> 00:14:39.470
Now I see. That's the bait they used
to land Chairman Ronan.

00:14:40.130 --> 00:14:43.050
They'll eliminate everyone who knows
the secret of the Box.

00:14:43.090 --> 00:14:46.720
That means the Vist Foundation and
Staff HQ found common ground.

00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:48.840
What are you planning to do?

00:14:48.880 --> 00:14:52.220
The General Revil is the key to
the reconstruction of Earth Fleet.

00:14:52.260 --> 00:14:55.380
If it attacked, the Nahel Argama
wouldn't stand a chance.

00:14:55.430 --> 00:14:58.090
If you're having trouble making
direct contact from your end,

00:14:58.130 --> 00:15:01.220
our people at Luio & Co. can pass
along the word that they're in danger.

00:15:01.260 --> 00:15:05.300
Beltorchika. I want to get in touch with
the camouflaged Sleeves freighter.

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:06.630
Captain?

00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:09.800
With Luio & Co. 's connections in
both the Federation and Neo Zeon,

00:15:09.840 --> 00:15:11.430
it should be doable.

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:13.760
Are you serious, Capt. Bright?

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:16.340
I have the perfect man
to act as negotiator.

00:15:16.380 --> 00:15:18.430
He hates Zeons with a passion, though.

00:15:22.840 --> 00:15:26.260
This is in your best interests, too, right?

00:15:26.300 --> 00:15:29.720
Or even a golden opportunity,
you might say. Well, I might anyway.

00:15:30.470 --> 00:15:33.180
Once the key to Laplace's Box is delivered,

00:15:33.220 --> 00:15:37.510
those Foundation people plan to take it
and your princess into space.

00:15:37.550 --> 00:15:39.800
If that happens, both of them will be
out of reach for good.

00:15:40.720 --> 00:15:43.550
How are we supposed to trust you?

00:15:43.590 --> 00:15:46.470
We don't like how the Vist Foundation
is conspiring with General Staff HQ

00:15:46.510 --> 00:15:49.590
and having the military
at their beck and call.

00:15:50.220 --> 00:15:52.510
A certain field commander
feels that way,

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:53.680
and there's also Luio & Co. ,

00:15:53.720 --> 00:15:56.430
which you can think of
as the Foundation's business rival.

00:15:57.720 --> 00:16:01.470
Whatever Laplace's Box really is, we don't
want to see the ties between

00:16:01.510 --> 00:16:05.260
the Federation and the Foundation
deepening as a result.

00:16:06.010 --> 00:16:09.800
And to keep that from happening, you'll
even make use of the Neo Zeon, eh?

00:16:09.840 --> 00:16:10.970
Captain...

00:16:11.630 --> 00:16:14.630
I want you to provide us
with one Base Jabber.

00:16:14.680 --> 00:16:15.930
I'll ask around.

00:16:15.970 --> 00:16:18.880
I take it this means you have a
guerilla-style way of doing this?

00:16:18.930 --> 00:16:22.010
The thing is, I'm just not sure we
can pull this off by ourselves.

00:16:22.050 --> 00:16:24.970
Even if we hit them with a sneak attack
and recapture the princess,

00:16:25.010 --> 00:16:27.550
it'll all be for nothing
if we can't escape.

00:16:27.590 --> 00:16:30.880
That's why I've been saying all along
that it will be a joint operation.

00:16:30.930 --> 00:16:32.930
I'll send reinforcements your way.

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:36.340
Even though it's a ship that you guys
share a nasty history with.

00:16:43.340 --> 00:16:48.300
In any case, the first order of business
in times such as this is to remain calm.

00:16:50.800 --> 00:16:53.630
It's been nearly 20 days since we
were ordered to remain on standby.

00:16:53.680 --> 00:16:55.680
It's understandable
that the men are irritated.

00:16:55.720 --> 00:16:58.880
However, you gentlemen,
their superior officers,

00:16:58.930 --> 00:17:01.380
must always
comport yourselves with- -

00:17:01.430 --> 00:17:02.430
Captain!

00:17:07.630 --> 00:17:08.720
Emergency message, sir!

00:17:38.010 --> 00:17:42.720
Don't laugh. I'm putting my money
on that boy's intuition.

00:17:59.340 --> 00:18:02.800
Why are they putting that pilot in it
during the transfer to the Garuda?

00:18:02.840 --> 00:18:05.760
Who can tell what
the top brass are thinking?

00:18:09.720 --> 00:18:12.380
Ensign Riddhe!
Where is Audrey?!

00:18:12.430 --> 00:18:16.260
You came down to Earth with her, right?!
Where is she?!

00:18:16.930 --> 00:18:17.880
Mr. Riddhe!

00:18:25.970 --> 00:18:27.840
I'm borrowing him for a minute.

00:18:34.380 --> 00:18:36.090
Careful, now!

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:39.380
If you trip on Earth,
you can get hurt.

00:18:41.010 --> 00:18:45.510
You guys don't get it, do you?
That man's the captain aboard this ship.

00:18:50.800 --> 00:18:51.880
Audrey's there?!

00:18:51.930 --> 00:18:53.340
No doubt about it.

00:18:53.880 --> 00:18:57.470
The Sleeves' Garencieres will carry out a
rescue operation

00:18:57.510 --> 00:18:59.340
during the Garuda transfer.

00:18:59.880 --> 00:19:01.800
Join the fight on their side.

00:19:02.590 --> 00:19:07.130
Go into space and rendezvous with the
Nahel Argama, which is coming to assist.

00:19:07.180 --> 00:19:11.180
That is the only way to keep the Box's key
out of the hands of the conspirators.

00:19:11.970 --> 00:19:14.430
The only way to save her.

00:19:15.430 --> 00:19:17.130
Can you do that?

00:19:17.180 --> 00:19:18.260
I'll do it.

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:21.050
This is all I can do for you.

00:19:23.130 --> 00:19:28.800
Just like every other Gundam pilot,
I like to think that it chose you.

00:19:32.260 --> 00:19:35.720
It was always the inevitable outcome.

00:19:37.130 --> 00:19:39.720
Be it good or bad.

00:19:40.220 --> 00:19:41.510
Capt. Bright...

00:19:42.090 --> 00:19:45.590
The rest is up to you.
Don't let the situation crush you.

00:19:54.010 --> 00:19:56.430
Be brave enough to fight off despair.

00:19:57.720 --> 00:20:03.470
If you're a Gundam pilot... a Newtype...
you can do it.

00:20:14.930 --> 00:20:16.180
Audrey...

00:20:18.340 --> 00:20:19.680
I'm coming!

00:20:31.470 --> 00:20:34.880
Allow me to express my admiration
for your pride.

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:40.380
However, that pride will get people killed.
Do you understand?

00:20:47.090 --> 00:20:49.970
At this very moment,
you have stolen the future

00:20:50.010 --> 00:20:53.760
from the Zeon survivors
who worship you.

00:20:53.800 --> 00:20:57.880
The only future they had where they
could coexist with the Vist Foundation.

00:21:00.970 --> 00:21:04.430
Women are more than capable of
killing men with their pride.

00:21:04.470 --> 00:21:06.430
You are blossoming into a fine woman.

00:21:06.470 --> 00:21:11.180
You are even turning that
Banagher Links boy into fertilizer.

00:21:16.680 --> 00:21:18.050
Banagher...

00:21:21.300 --> 00:21:24.090
What did the Captain say to that kid?

00:21:24.130 --> 00:21:26.680
I don't want to get caught up
in any weird ruckuses.

00:21:26.720 --> 00:21:28.680
Do you think the Young Master knows?

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:31.590
Nah. He's probably in the dark, too.

00:21:31.630 --> 00:21:33.550
But Capt. Bright knows what he's doing.

00:21:33.590 --> 00:21:35.260
Don't panic, whatever happens.

00:21:38.800 --> 00:21:40.180
Ensign Riddhe.

00:21:40.800 --> 00:21:45.800
Keep an eye on the Unicorn.
Keeping it safe will help you as well.

00:21:46.800 --> 00:21:49.470
Your father's decisions are his alone.

00:21:49.510 --> 00:21:53.090
You're young.
Act according to your own judgment.

00:21:53.130 --> 00:21:54.220
Understood.

00:21:55.300 --> 00:21:57.220
You don't need to tell me that...

00:21:58.930 --> 00:22:01.380
Not if Mineva is there.

00:22:01.430 --> 00:22:02.630
We're leaving!

00:23:38.300 --> 00:23:41.430
Next time, on Mobile Suit Gundam Unicorn

00:23:41.470 --> 00:23:44.380
CLASH OF THE TWO UNICORNS

00:23:45.050 --> 00:23:48.430
awaken the Newtype that lies within you.
